## Root cause

Guarded release PRs set `pages/deploy` status on the PR head, but the trusted `workflow_dispatch` runs `deploy.yml` from `main` and `actions/checkout` had no `ref`. The job therefore built current `main`, not the requested release SHA. This is why PR #155 had green exact-head CI while Pages validation failed before Vite.

## Permanent provenance contract

- dispatcher reads `public/brand-release.txt` from the exact same-repo PR head;
- release id and master SHA-256 are passed as typed workflow inputs;
- Pages validates that the SHA is the current head of an open `deploy-live-*` PR targeting `main`;
- checkout is detached at that exact SHA with persisted credentials disabled;
- `git rev-parse HEAD` must equal the requested SHA before dependencies or scripts run;
- release proof is derived from checked-out `dist/brand-release.txt`, not hardcoded v2/v3 workflow constants;
- build outputs carry the exact release id/hash into custom-domain verification;
- ordinary pushes to `main` remain supported.

## Scope

