## Root cause

The retained reduced-motion iPhone screenshot from merged PR #162 was background-only even though the test's computed-state JSON reported the complete final state.

Temporary diagnostic PR #168 captured the exact production build at seven WebKit paint stages. Its artifact (`sha256:8c72273f7c32a63039fbbb4332387904c26c0ccdf92efcf76700168f9e733413`) proved:

- all six portraits were decoded;
- hero/title/window opacity was already `1`;
- transforms and filters were already final;
- no animations remained;
- the immediate page screenshot was blank;
- after two `requestAnimationFrame` callbacks the complete first viewport painted correctly;
- 250 ms, 1000 ms, animation cancellation/inline finalization and display/reflow produced the same result as two frames;
- the direct hero element screenshot was correct.

This is a Playwright/WebKit first-paint screenshot race, not a production rendering defect.

## Fix

The existing reduced-motion test keeps all current computed-state assertions and then calls the already established `afterPaint(page)` helper before writing the screenshot evidence. No timeout, sleep or product workaround is added.

